{"sha":"1b86129be1f0285c403616cb362ac188de676c6e","node_id":"C_kwDOIbbQxNoAKDFiODYxMjliZTFmMDI4NWM0MDM2MTZjYjM2MmFjMTg4ZGU2NzZjNmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mend Renovate","email":"bot@renovateapp.com","date":"2026-10-02T05:16:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-10-02T05:16:32Z"},"message":"fix(deps): update osv-scanner minor (#3067)\n\nThis PR contains the following updates:\n\n| Package | Change |\n[Age](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) |\n[Confidence](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n|\n[github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk)\n| `v1.7.0` → `v1.8.0` |\n![age](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/age/go/github.com%2fmodelcontextprotocol%2fgo-sdk/v1.8.0?slim=true)\n|\n![confidence](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/confidence/go/github.com%2fmodelcontextprotocol%2fgo-sdk/v1.7.0/v1.8.0?slim=true)\n|\n| [github.com/urfave/cli/v3](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli) |\n`v3.11.0` → `v3.13.0` |\n![age](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/age/go/github.com%2furfave%2fcli%2fv3/v3.13.0?slim=true)\n|\n![confidence](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/confidence/go/github.com%2furfave%2fcli%2fv3/v3.11.0/v3.13.0?slim=true)\n|\n| [google.golang.org/grpc](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go) |\n`v1.83.2` → `v1.84.0` |\n![age](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/age/go/google.golang.org%2fgrpc/v1.84.0?slim=true)\n|\n![confidence](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/confidence/go/google.golang.org%2fgrpc/v1.83.2/v1.84.0?slim=true)\n|\n\n---\n\n### Release Notes\n\n<details>\n<summary>modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk\n(github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk)</summary>\n\n###\n[`v1.8.0`](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/releases/tag/v1.8.0)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/compare/v1.7.0...v1.8.0)\n\n***This release is equivalent to v1.8.0-pre.2. Thank you to those who\ntested the pre-release.***\n\nIn this release we introduce several fixes and improvements on top of\n[v1.7.0](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/releases/tag/v1.7.0).\nIt adds no new protocol revision: the supported set is unchanged, and\n`2026-07-28` remains the newest version the SDK negotiates.\n\nThe bulk of the work is hardening the transports against resource\nexhaustion, closing session leaks, deadlocks and teardown hangs found by\nusers running the new protocol at scale, and giving servers explicit\ncontrol over which protocol versions they advertise.\n\nTwo behavior changes are guarded by new `MCPGODEBUG` flags; see the\nsection below.\n\n#### Hardening against resource exhaustion\n\nEvery decoding path that buffers incoming input is now bounded. JSON\npayloads are rejected past 1000 levels of nesting, before the parser\nrecurses. Both SSE readers cap the bytes buffered for a single event via\n`MaxEventSize` on `SSEClientTransport` and `StreamableClientTransport`,\nand the stdio transport caps a single JSON-RPC frame via\n`StdioTransport.MaxLineLength`.\n\nOn the OAuth side, dynamic client registration responses are bounded to\n1 MB, and the discovery code now validates metadata documents rather\nthan trusting them.\n\n- internal/json: json nesting depth check by\n[@&#8203;yarolegovich](https://redirect.github.com/yarolegovich)\n([#&#8203;1200](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1200))\n- mcp: add an sse event size cap by\n[@&#8203;yarolegovich](https://redirect.github.com/yarolegovich)\n([#&#8203;1205](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1205))\n- mcp: add a max request body size of the old transport by\n[@&#8203;yarolegovich](https://redirect.github.com/yarolegovich)\n([#&#8203;1224](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1224))\n- oauthex: bound dcr read to 1mb by\n[@&#8203;yarolegovich](https://redirect.github.com/yarolegovich)\n([#&#8203;1206](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1206))\n- oauthex: oauth discovery checks by\n[@&#8203;yarolegovich](https://redirect.github.com/yarolegovich)\n([#&#8203;1220](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1220))\n\n#### Restricting the protocol versions a server supports\n\n`ServerOptions.SupportedProtocolVersions` lets a server narrow the set\nof versions it advertises and negotiates. The list can only narrow,\nnever widen; naming a version the SDK does not implement panics at\nconstruction.\nRelatedly, a stateful streamable handler receiving a `2026-07-28`\nrequest now returns that same JSON-RPC error instead of a plain-text\n400, so the client can renegotiate down instead of losing the\nconnection.\n\n- mcp: allow restricting the protocol versions a server supports by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1199](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1199))\n- mcp: return json-rpc error on stateful server serving\nprotocolVersion20260728 requests by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1143](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1143))\n- mcp: limit SSE discover supportedVersions to SSE-defined revisions by\n[@&#8203;arimu1](https://redirect.github.com/arimu1)\n([#&#8203;1121](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1121))\n- mcp: prefer the negotiated protocol version over the request context\nby [@&#8203;gwyszynski-sa](https://redirect.github.com/gwyszynski-sa)\n([#&#8203;1163](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1163))\n- mcp: export ClientSessionOptions.ProtocolVersion by\n[@&#8203;arimu1](https://redirect.github.com/arimu1)\n([#&#8203;1127](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1127))\n\n#### Per-request cache control\n\n`ServerOptions.SetCacheable` is a new hook that decides the `ttlMs` and\n`cacheScope` fields of every result carrying them: `server/discover`,\nthe four list methods, and `resources/read`. It runs once per result,\nafter the handler returns, with the values that handler produced, so it\ncan set a policy globally while still letting an individual handler\noverride it. Anything left unset falls back to the protocol default of\n`public`.\n\n- mcp: allow per request Cacheable customization by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1203](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1203))\n\n#### Behavior changes guarded by MCPGODEBUG\n\nTwo new escape-hatch flags restore the previous behavior of the changes\nabove. Both will be removed in **v1.9.0**.\n\n- **`plaintextstatefulrejection=1`** — restore the plain-text\n`http.Error` 400 body a stateful `StreamableHTTPHandler` previously\nreturned for a request carrying per-request metadata. The default is now\na JSON-RPC `-32022 CodeUnsupportedProtocolVersion` error with an\n`UnsupportedProtocolVersionData` payload advertising the legacy versions\nthe server supports. Introduced by\n[#&#8203;1143](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1143).\n- **`blockingcancelnotify=1`** — restore the previous behavior where a\ncancelled call waits synchronously for `notifications/cancelled` to be\ndelivered (up to 5s) before returning, joining any delivery error into\nthe caller's error. The default now retires the call immediately and\nsends the notification asynchronously. Introduced by\n[#&#8203;1151](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1151).\n\nOptions below were removed, according to plan:\n\n- `seterroroverwrite`\n- `enableoriginverification`\n- `disablecontenttypecheck`\n- `disablelocalhostprotection`\n\n#### Other Changes to the SDK\n\n- mcp: fix ListTools panic and null normalization on malformed tools by\n[@&#8203;n0liu](https://redirect.github.com/n0liu)\n([#&#8203;1120](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1120))\n- mcp: avoid panicking when a resource handler returns nil by\n[@&#8203;latent-9](https://redirect.github.com/latent-9)\n([#&#8203;1176](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1176))\n- mcp: prevent MemoryEventStore.After panic on index past the end by\n[@&#8203;PratikDhanave](https://redirect.github.com/PratikDhanave)\n([#&#8203;1132](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1132))\n- internal/jsonrpc2: test WireError.Is and fix nil target panic by\n[@&#8203;aha-jansen](https://redirect.github.com/aha-jansen)\n([#&#8203;1079](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1079))\n- jsonrpc2: wrap write error in server-closing error by\n[@&#8203;Tethys0](https://redirect.github.com/Tethys0)\n([#&#8203;1186](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1186))\n- internal/jsonrpc2: plumb cancellation cause through request context by\n[@&#8203;aha-jansen](https://redirect.github.com/aha-jansen)\n([#&#8203;1103](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1103))\n- mcp: preserve single-request batch responses by\n[@&#8203;wmh123wmh1](https://redirect.github.com/wmh123wmh1)\n([#&#8203;1214](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1214))\n- mcp: don't mutate caller params on multi-round-trip retries by\n[@&#8203;yhxlele](https://redirect.github.com/yhxlele)\n([#&#8203;1145](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1145))\n- mcp: do not check metatada on notifications by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1215](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1215))\n- fix: only subscribe when server advertises capability by\n[@&#8203;yarolegovich](https://redirect.github.com/yarolegovich)\n([#&#8203;1221](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1221))\n- mcp: tolerate 404 on subscriptions/listen in stateless mode by\n[@&#8203;smlx](https://redirect.github.com/smlx)\n([#&#8203;1193](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1193))\n- mcp: keep request log levels scoped to each request by\n[@&#8203;jstar0](https://redirect.github.com/jstar0)\n([#&#8203;1168](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1168))\n- mcp: add docs for tier 1 assessment by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1195](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1195))\n- docs: make the protocol.md table of contents resolve by\n[@&#8203;tonydzi](https://redirect.github.com/tonydzi)\n([#&#8203;1196](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1196))\n- docs: fix the streamable client snippet to use (\\*Client).Connect by\n[@&#8203;tonydzi](https://redirect.github.com/tonydzi)\n([#&#8203;1142](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1142))\n- docs: quick start `go get` leaves the module unbuildable by\n[@&#8203;tonydzi](https://redirect.github.com/tonydzi)\n([#&#8203;1148](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1148))\n- docs: fix four dead links to the Multi Round-Trip Requests section by\n[@&#8203;tonydzi](https://redirect.github.com/tonydzi)\n([#&#8203;1159](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1159))\n- mcp: fix typo in protocol version comment by\n[@&#8203;latent-9](https://redirect.github.com/latent-9)\n([#&#8203;1156](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1156))\n- mcp: fix ListChanged doc comments on server capabilities by\n[@&#8203;qhzhu](https://redirect.github.com/qhzhu)\n([#&#8203;1219](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1219))\n- mcp: add ServerSession.NotifyElicitationComplete by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1194](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1194))\n- mcp: update conformance tests by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1231](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1231))\n- Disable scheduled nightly runs on forks by\n[@&#8203;IAmSurajBobade](https://redirect.github.com/IAmSurajBobade)\n([#&#8203;1083](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1083))\n- auth: add ScopeFilter hook to AuthorizationCodeHandlerConfig by\n[@&#8203;toabctl](https://redirect.github.com/toabctl)\n([#&#8203;1044](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1044))\n- auth: validate unadvertised RFC 9207 iss instead of rejecting it by\n[@&#8203;asjdf](https://redirect.github.com/asjdf)\n([#&#8203;1187](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1187))\n- mcp: prevent leaks of ServerSession on StatefulServer by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1137](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1137))\n- mcp: avoid Client.Connect leaks by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1158](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1158))\n- mcp: resolve deadlock on serverSession.Close() with\nsubscriptionsListen call by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1166](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1166))\n- mcp: prune completed listen request IDs from the session by\n[@&#8203;latent-9](https://redirect.github.com/latent-9)\n([#&#8203;1190](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1190))\n- mcp: bound streamable Close DELETE so a silent peer cannot hang\nteardown by [@&#8203;LPX-E5BD8](https://redirect.github.com/LPX-E5BD8)\n([#&#8203;1184](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1184))\n- mcp: allow asynchronous cancel notification by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1151](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1151))\n- mcp: fix error propagation to prevent session closing by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1118](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1118))\n- refactor: remove legacy MCPGODEBUG compatibility for new protocol\nrelease by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n- build(deps): bump the codeql-action group with 3 updates by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1122](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1122))\n- build(deps): bump the codeql-action group with 3 updates by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1216](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1216))\n- build(deps): bump `actions/setup-node` from 6.0.0 to 7.0.0 by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1123](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1123))\n- build(deps): bump `actions/setup-python` from 6.3.0 to 7.0.0 by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1124](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1124))\n- build(deps): bump `actions/setup-go` from 6.5.0 to 7.0.0 by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1125](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1125))\n- build(deps): bump `actions/checkout` from 7.0.0 to 7.0.1 by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1126](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1126))\n- build(deps): bump `golang/govulncheck-action` from 1.0.4 to 1.1.0 by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1218](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1218))\n- build(deps): bump `ossf/scorecard-action` from 2.4.3 to 2.4.4 by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1217](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1217))\n\n#### New Contributors\n\n- [@&#8203;n0liu](https://redirect.github.com/n0liu) made their first\ncontribution in\n[#&#8203;1120](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1120)\n- [@&#8203;arimu1](https://redirect.github.com/arimu1) made their first\ncontribution in\n[#&#8203;1127](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1127)\n- [@&#8203;tonydzi](https://redirect.github.com/tonydzi) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;1142](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1142)\n- [@&#8203;latent-9](https://redirect.github.com/latent-9) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;1156](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1156)\n- [@&#8203;jstar0](https://redirect.github.com/jstar0) made their first\ncontribution in\n[#&#8203;1168](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1168)\n- [@&#8203;gwyszynski-sa](https://redirect.github.com/gwyszynski-sa)\nmade their first contribution in\n[#&#8203;1163](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1163)\n- [@&#8203;aha-jansen](https://redirect.github.com/aha-jansen) made\ntheir first contribution in\n[#&#8203;1103](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1103)\n- [@&#8203;PratikDhanave](https://redirect.github.com/PratikDhanave)\nmade their first contribution in\n[#&#8203;1132](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1132)\n- [@&#8203;LPX-E5BD8](https://redirect.github.com/LPX-E5BD8) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;1184](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1184)\n- [@&#8203;asjdf](https://redirect.github.com/asjdf) made their first\ncontribution in\n[#&#8203;1187](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1187)\n- [@&#8203;Tethys0](https://redirect.github.com/Tethys0) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;1186](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1186)\n- [@&#8203;wmh123wmh1](https://redirect.github.com/wmh123wmh1) made\ntheir first contribution in\n[#&#8203;1214](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1214)\n- [@&#8203;yhxlele](https://redirect.github.com/yhxlele) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;1145](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1145)\n- [@&#8203;qhzhu](https://redirect.github.com/qhzhu) made their first\ncontribution in\n[#&#8203;1219](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1219)\n\n**Full Changelog**:\n<https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/compare/v1.7.0...v1.8.0-pre.1>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>urfave/cli (github.com/urfave/cli/v3)</summary>\n\n###\n[`v3.13.0`](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/releases/tag/v3.13.0)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/compare/v3.12.0...v3.13.0)\n\n#### What's Changed\n\n- Trim the key of a map flag when TrimSpace is set by\n[@&#8203;youdie006](https://redirect.github.com/youdie006) in\n[#&#8203;2431](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2431)\n- Fix inverse bool flag counting with an external counter by\n[@&#8203;jakezwang](https://redirect.github.com/jakezwang) in\n[#&#8203;2432](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2432)\n- feat: add Deprecated field to flags and commands by\n[@&#8203;anandghegde](https://redirect.github.com/anandghegde) in\n[#&#8203;2429](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2429)\n- fix: parse single-rune Unicode flags by\n[@&#8203;znnnnnnn-wil](https://redirect.github.com/znnnnnnn-wil) in\n[#&#8203;2434](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2434)\n\n#### New Contributors\n\n- [@&#8203;jakezwang](https://redirect.github.com/jakezwang) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;2432](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2432)\n- [@&#8203;anandghegde](https://redirect.github.com/anandghegde) made\ntheir first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2429](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2429)\n- [@&#8203;znnnnnnn-wil](https://redirect.github.com/znnnnnnn-wil) made\ntheir first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2434](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2434)\n\n**Full Changelog**:\n<https://github.com/urfave/cli/compare/v3.12.0...v3.13.0>\n\n###\n[`v3.12.0`](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/releases/tag/v3.12.0)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/compare/v3.11.0...v3.12.0)\n\n#### What's Changed\n\n- feat: add Command.ArgValidator for tree-wide argument validation by\n[@&#8203;dearchap](https://redirect.github.com/dearchap) in\n[#&#8203;2377](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2377)\n- Single-value arguments can be marked as required by\n[@&#8203;idelchi](https://redirect.github.com/idelchi) in\n[#&#8203;2393](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2393)\n- docs: clarify that named Arguments are excluded from cmd.Args() by\n[@&#8203;dearchap](https://redirect.github.com/dearchap) in\n[#&#8203;2411](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2411)\n- fix: never run command action on shell completion past a double dash\nby [@&#8203;dearchap](https://redirect.github.com/dearchap) in\n[#&#8203;2412](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2412)\n- chore(deps): bump github.com/stretchr/testify from 1.11.1 to 1.12.0 by\n[@&#8203;app/dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/app/dependabot) in\n[#&#8203;2413](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2413)\n- Support custom FlagStringer for MutuallyExclusiveFlags by\n[@&#8203;SHIVANSHGARG07](https://redirect.github.com/SHIVANSHGARG07) in\n[#&#8203;2414](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2414)\n- Add TextFlag for encoding.TextMarshaler/TextUnmarshaler values by\n[@&#8203;ChrisJr404](https://redirect.github.com/ChrisJr404) in\n[#&#8203;2415](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2415)\n- chore(deps): bump github.com/stretchr/testify from 1.12.0 to 1.12.1 by\n[@&#8203;app/dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/app/dependabot) in\n[#&#8203;2416](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2416)\n- chore(deps): bump the python-packages group with 2 updates by\n[@&#8203;app/dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/app/dependabot) in\n[#&#8203;2417](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2417)\n- Show inherited persistent flags in child help by\n[@&#8203;justadityaraj](https://redirect.github.com/justadityaraj) in\n[#&#8203;2421](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2421)\n- fix: preserve whitespace in positional arguments by\n[@&#8203;lenamonj](https://redirect.github.com/lenamonj) in\n[#&#8203;2423](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2423)\n- fix: preserve whitespace in equals-form flag values by\n[@&#8203;BenYang12](https://redirect.github.com/BenYang12) in\n[#&#8203;2425](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2425)\n- fix: complete subcommand flags after positional arguments by\n[@&#8203;fzlzjerry](https://redirect.github.com/fzlzjerry) in\n[#&#8203;2426](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2426)\n- Fix a year-less timestamp layout losing January 1 by\n[@&#8203;youdie006](https://redirect.github.com/youdie006) in\n[#&#8203;2427](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2427)\n- docs: add go-size-analyzer, module version, and reflection by\n[@&#8203;imsumedhaa](https://redirect.github.com/imsumedhaa) in\n[#&#8203;2428](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2428)\n\n#### New Contributors\n\n- [@&#8203;idelchi](https://redirect.github.com/idelchi) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;2393](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2393)\n- [@&#8203;SHIVANSHGARG07](https://redirect.github.com/SHIVANSHGARG07)\nmade their first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2414](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2414)\n- [@&#8203;ChrisJr404](https://redirect.github.com/ChrisJr404) made\ntheir first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2415](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2415)\n- [@&#8203;justadityaraj](https://redirect.github.com/justadityaraj)\nmade their first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2421](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2421)\n- [@&#8203;lenamonj](https://redirect.github.com/lenamonj) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;2423](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2423)\n- [@&#8203;BenYang12](https://redirect.github.com/BenYang12) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;2425](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2425)\n- [@&#8203;youdie006](https://redirect.github.com/youdie006) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;2427](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2427)\n- [@&#8203;imsumedhaa](https://redirect.github.com/imsumedhaa) made\ntheir first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2428](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2428)\n\n**Full Changelog**:\n<https://github.com/urfave/cli/compare/v3.11.0...v3.12.0>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>grpc/grpc-go (google.golang.org/grpc)</summary>\n\n###\n[`v1.84.0`](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/releases/tag/v1.84.0):\nRelease 1.84.0\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/compare/v1.83.2...v1.84.0)\n\n### Behavior Changes\n\n- stats/otel: The `grpc.lb.pick_first.*` metrics have been removed and\nreplaced with `grpc.subchannel.*` metrics. See [gRFC\nA94](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/proposal/blob/master/A94-subchannel-otel-metrics.md)\nfor more details.\n([#&#8203;9215](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9215))\n\n### New Features\n\n- xds: Add support for `contains_match` in route header matchers.\n([#&#8203;9223](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9223))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- client: Fix a bug where a `ClientConn` could get permanently stuck in\nIDLE when an RPC was canceled during stream creation. Previously, such\ncancellations triggered stream cleanup twice, corrupting the channel's\nidleness state and causing subsequent RPCs to fail with deadline\nexceeded errors.\n([#&#8203;9191](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9191))\n- Special Thanks:\n[@&#8203;utkuozdemir](https://redirect.github.com/utkuozdemir)\n- client: Fix a bug where non-gRPC HTTP responses ending with an empty\nDATA frame failed the RPC with status code `Internal` instead of\npreserving the HTTP-mapped status code and response body.\n([#&#8203;9217](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9217))\n- Special Thanks:\n[@&#8203;chengxilo](https://redirect.github.com/chengxilo)\n- credentials: Validate metadata returned by per-RPC credentials,\nfailing the RPC with status code `Internal` if invalid keys or values\nare found. Previously, invalid metadata from credentials was sent to the\nserver in outgoing HTTP/2 requests.\n([#&#8203;9202](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9202))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;buger](https://redirect.github.com/buger)\n- credentials/sts: Prevent potential token leakage by disallowing HTTP\nredirects during STS token exchange. Previously, 3xx redirects were\nfollowed automatically, replaying the request body containing\nauthentication tokens to the redirect destination.\n([#&#8203;9299](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9299))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n- randomsubsetting: Ignore endpoints that contain no addresses.\nPreviously, this could cause the policy to panic while computing hashes.\n([#&#8203;9259](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9259))\n- Special Thanks:\n[@&#8203;fallintoplace](https://redirect.github.com/fallintoplace)\n- stats/otel: Ensure method names are populated in trace spans when\nmetrics are disabled. Previously, running with tracing enabled and\nmetrics disabled resulted in server trace spans lacking the RPC method\nname (recording only \"Recv.\").\n([#&#8203;9262](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9262))\n- transport: Return `io.ErrUnexpectedEOF` when EOF is encountered after\npartial header or message body reads. Previously, partial reads could\nreturn a plain `io.EOF`, failing to distinguish truncated data from a\nclean end of stream.\n([#&#8203;9204](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9204))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;buger](https://redirect.github.com/buger)\n- transport: Validate metadata supplied by balancers (in\n`PickResult.Metadata`) and resolver addresses, failing the RPC with\nstatus code `Internal` if invalid keys or values are found. Previously,\ninvalid metadata from these sources was sent to the server in outgoing\nHTTP/2 requests.\n([#&#8203;9203](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9203))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;buger](https://redirect.github.com/buger)\n- xds: Fix a rare corner case that could prevent a cluster from being\nremoved when it is no longer in use.\n([#&#8203;9140](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9140))\n- xds: Fix panic during route matching for routes containing header\nmatchers with empty `exact_match` strings.\n([#&#8203;9223](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9223))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n- xds: Reject routes containing header matchers with empty\n`prefix_match` or `suffix_match` strings. Previously, this caused a\npanic during route matching.\n([#&#8203;9223](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9223))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n- xds: Fix EDS drop policies being applied at a much lower rate than\nconfigured due to an integer overflow.\n([#&#8203;9257](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9257))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n- xds: Reject EDS resources containing drop policies with unsupported\ndenominators. Previously, such resources caused the client to panic when\ncalculating drop rates.\n([#&#8203;9218](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9218))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n- xds/rbac: Reject RBAC configurations containing nested `Principal` or\n`Permission` rules with `:scheme` or `grpc-` prefixed header matchers.\nPreviously, such configurations could cause DENY policies to fail open.\n([#&#8203;9258](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9258))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n- xds/rbac: Rewrite `host` header matchers to `:authority` in nested\n`Principal` and `Permission` rules. Previously, this rewrite only\napplied to top-level rules, causing nested `host` matchers to never\nmatch incoming requests and DENY policies to fail open.\n([#&#8203;9258](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9258))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n- xds/rbac: Reject `CidrRanges` with an unset prefix length. Previously,\nan omitted `prefix_len` field caused a panic during RBAC configuration\nparsing.\n([#&#8203;9250](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9250))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n\n### Performance Improvements\n\n- transport: Avoid a heap allocation when flushing shared write buffers.\n([#&#8203;9233](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9233))\n- Special Thanks:\n[@&#8203;zaidoon1](https://redirect.github.com/zaidoon1)\n- credentials/alts: Support dynamic frame size negotiation and add the\n`GRPC_GO_EXPERIMENTAL_ALTS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE` environment variable (default\n4KiB, max 512KiB) to configure the maximum ALTS record frame size.\n([#&#8203;9268](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9268))\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Configuration\n\n📅 **Schedule**: (in timezone Australia/Sydney)\n\n- Branch creation\n  - \"before 6am on monday\"\n- Automerge\n  - At any time (no schedule defined)\n\n🚦 **Automerge**: Disabled by config. Please merge this manually once you\nare satisfied.\n\n♻ **Rebasing**: Whenever PR becomes conflicted, or you tick the\nrebase/retry checkbox.\n\n👻 **Immortal**: This PR will be recreated if closed unmerged. Get\n[config\nhelp](https://redirect.github.com/renovatebot/renovate/discussions) if\nthat's undesired.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] <!-- rebase-check -->If you want to rebase/retry this PR, check\nthis box\n\n---\n\nThis PR was generated by [Mend Renovate](https://mend.io/renovate/).\nView the [repository job\nlog](https://developer.mend.io/github/google/osv-scanner).\n\n<!--renovate-debug:eyJjcmVhdGVkSW5WZXIiOiI0NC43MS4wIiwidXBkYXRlZEluVmVyIjoiNDQuMTEyLjAiLCJ0YXJnZXRCcmFuY2giOiJtYWluIiwibGFiZWxzIjpbImRlcGVuZGVuY2llcyJdfQ==-->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Rex P <rexpan@google.com>","tree":{"sha":"340589c6f3747774f7b25c025fd9a39c77e2d60b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/osv-scanner/git/trees/340589c6f3747774f7b25c025fd9a39c77e2d60b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/osv-scanner/git/commits/1b86129be1f0285c403616cb362ac188de676c6e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvz4wCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAc2cQAFn4/XJ87Q4WfJxIZy98Zabq\nU7f21lQvx7JvpRIFcpAdRN69coShPTmAiluIMKE4QDzWPeORmArN7x6g2+f7Nk6R\nxEuyyr0XXMxW/KX/wfkx6zGenOHAPoAQctaLKKiUm4y6XFPdNAoYY1k5ajGU4ZbA\ncxCbAhEnes/VrUd6B0U7xBKROTazgxWHCKO8+X5Xom5Hvr/iCBupC7YHjsUoOX8E\nSC6BT+sEtWF3J7Mv3EzIA/L+N1zk4KqPsMDd/P73CaWGTEueQfZ1jcYKL24NFvxO\nOE2V4ZdGuLfEQhzRBWbZ8PGEQuXHgX/B/to4Ud+PHucZxsB/LrbTG0yYRBHXROvT\noK2VlB6NsVr6brFcSiFXM7dbK5gRoOe2uCzLPynFIaWrNWQNEbia3TUczCyBwSxf\nfV9+cJRZvUPU9hQi8DQC+jQPyhChIzQ9o4YCi3t7BiBI+aC0l0BtImx7GlDASkhp\nNdyIE24adFQOAF8SUEnioUDSSdE7Lr/aIeOYfA2VGVnPdn0Xn95tsYSZbxvRlXxw\nO0cJOxFjim0hrE/wNfg02ngyojQHOhqcKwDnaaaVJL+lgLx1fP65/Dl2nRVRzRcN\nShcoJiES9lzNFFFj8nORJ3Zq+rfU6No20Xg+ilwSskOWDpCEFwfLI5UT9HbgDrkx\nAxzeLxArA2vItY2bUnE3\n=lhIA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 340589c6f3747774f7b25c025fd9a39c77e2d60b\nparent eb6f0e10e76b9fac503af73556cba2528773062d\nauthor Mend Renovate <bot@renovateapp.com> 1790918192 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790918192 +1000\n\nfix(deps): update osv-scanner minor (#3067)\n\nThis PR contains the following updates:\n\n| Package | Change |\n[Age](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) |\n[Confidence](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n|\n[github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk)\n| `v1.7.0` → `v1.8.0` |\n![age](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/age/go/github.com%2fmodelcontextprotocol%2fgo-sdk/v1.8.0?slim=true)\n|\n![confidence](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/confidence/go/github.com%2fmodelcontextprotocol%2fgo-sdk/v1.7.0/v1.8.0?slim=true)\n|\n| [github.com/urfave/cli/v3](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli) |\n`v3.11.0` → `v3.13.0` |\n![age](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/age/go/github.com%2furfave%2fcli%2fv3/v3.13.0?slim=true)\n|\n![confidence](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/confidence/go/github.com%2furfave%2fcli%2fv3/v3.11.0/v3.13.0?slim=true)\n|\n| [google.golang.org/grpc](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go) |\n`v1.83.2` → `v1.84.0` |\n![age](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/age/go/google.golang.org%2fgrpc/v1.84.0?slim=true)\n|\n![confidence](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/confidence/go/google.golang.org%2fgrpc/v1.83.2/v1.84.0?slim=true)\n|\n\n---\n\n### Release Notes\n\n<details>\n<summary>modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk\n(github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk)</summary>\n\n###\n[`v1.8.0`](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/releases/tag/v1.8.0)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/compare/v1.7.0...v1.8.0)\n\n***This release is equivalent to v1.8.0-pre.2. Thank you to those who\ntested the pre-release.***\n\nIn this release we introduce several fixes and improvements on top of\n[v1.7.0](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/releases/tag/v1.7.0).\nIt adds no new protocol revision: the supported set is unchanged, and\n`2026-07-28` remains the newest version the SDK negotiates.\n\nThe bulk of the work is hardening the transports against resource\nexhaustion, closing session leaks, deadlocks and teardown hangs found by\nusers running the new protocol at scale, and giving servers explicit\ncontrol over which protocol versions they advertise.\n\nTwo behavior changes are guarded by new `MCPGODEBUG` flags; see the\nsection below.\n\n#### Hardening against resource exhaustion\n\nEvery decoding path that buffers incoming input is now bounded. JSON\npayloads are rejected past 1000 levels of nesting, before the parser\nrecurses. Both SSE readers cap the bytes buffered for a single event via\n`MaxEventSize` on `SSEClientTransport` and `StreamableClientTransport`,\nand the stdio transport caps a single JSON-RPC frame via\n`StdioTransport.MaxLineLength`.\n\nOn the OAuth side, dynamic client registration responses are bounded to\n1 MB, and the discovery code now validates metadata documents rather\nthan trusting them.\n\n- internal/json: json nesting depth check by\n[@&#8203;yarolegovich](https://redirect.github.com/yarolegovich)\n([#&#8203;1200](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1200))\n- mcp: add an sse event size cap by\n[@&#8203;yarolegovich](https://redirect.github.com/yarolegovich)\n([#&#8203;1205](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1205))\n- mcp: add a max request body size of the old transport by\n[@&#8203;yarolegovich](https://redirect.github.com/yarolegovich)\n([#&#8203;1224](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1224))\n- oauthex: bound dcr read to 1mb by\n[@&#8203;yarolegovich](https://redirect.github.com/yarolegovich)\n([#&#8203;1206](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1206))\n- oauthex: oauth discovery checks by\n[@&#8203;yarolegovich](https://redirect.github.com/yarolegovich)\n([#&#8203;1220](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1220))\n\n#### Restricting the protocol versions a server supports\n\n`ServerOptions.SupportedProtocolVersions` lets a server narrow the set\nof versions it advertises and negotiates. The list can only narrow,\nnever widen; naming a version the SDK does not implement panics at\nconstruction.\nRelatedly, a stateful streamable handler receiving a `2026-07-28`\nrequest now returns that same JSON-RPC error instead of a plain-text\n400, so the client can renegotiate down instead of losing the\nconnection.\n\n- mcp: allow restricting the protocol versions a server supports by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1199](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1199))\n- mcp: return json-rpc error on stateful server serving\nprotocolVersion20260728 requests by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1143](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1143))\n- mcp: limit SSE discover supportedVersions to SSE-defined revisions by\n[@&#8203;arimu1](https://redirect.github.com/arimu1)\n([#&#8203;1121](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1121))\n- mcp: prefer the negotiated protocol version over the request context\nby [@&#8203;gwyszynski-sa](https://redirect.github.com/gwyszynski-sa)\n([#&#8203;1163](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1163))\n- mcp: export ClientSessionOptions.ProtocolVersion by\n[@&#8203;arimu1](https://redirect.github.com/arimu1)\n([#&#8203;1127](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1127))\n\n#### Per-request cache control\n\n`ServerOptions.SetCacheable` is a new hook that decides the `ttlMs` and\n`cacheScope` fields of every result carrying them: `server/discover`,\nthe four list methods, and `resources/read`. It runs once per result,\nafter the handler returns, with the values that handler produced, so it\ncan set a policy globally while still letting an individual handler\noverride it. Anything left unset falls back to the protocol default of\n`public`.\n\n- mcp: allow per request Cacheable customization by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1203](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1203))\n\n#### Behavior changes guarded by MCPGODEBUG\n\nTwo new escape-hatch flags restore the previous behavior of the changes\nabove. Both will be removed in **v1.9.0**.\n\n- **`plaintextstatefulrejection=1`** — restore the plain-text\n`http.Error` 400 body a stateful `StreamableHTTPHandler` previously\nreturned for a request carrying per-request metadata. The default is now\na JSON-RPC `-32022 CodeUnsupportedProtocolVersion` error with an\n`UnsupportedProtocolVersionData` payload advertising the legacy versions\nthe server supports. Introduced by\n[#&#8203;1143](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1143).\n- **`blockingcancelnotify=1`** — restore the previous behavior where a\ncancelled call waits synchronously for `notifications/cancelled` to be\ndelivered (up to 5s) before returning, joining any delivery error into\nthe caller's error. The default now retires the call immediately and\nsends the notification asynchronously. Introduced by\n[#&#8203;1151](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1151).\n\nOptions below were removed, according to plan:\n\n- `seterroroverwrite`\n- `enableoriginverification`\n- `disablecontenttypecheck`\n- `disablelocalhostprotection`\n\n#### Other Changes to the SDK\n\n- mcp: fix ListTools panic and null normalization on malformed tools by\n[@&#8203;n0liu](https://redirect.github.com/n0liu)\n([#&#8203;1120](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1120))\n- mcp: avoid panicking when a resource handler returns nil by\n[@&#8203;latent-9](https://redirect.github.com/latent-9)\n([#&#8203;1176](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1176))\n- mcp: prevent MemoryEventStore.After panic on index past the end by\n[@&#8203;PratikDhanave](https://redirect.github.com/PratikDhanave)\n([#&#8203;1132](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1132))\n- internal/jsonrpc2: test WireError.Is and fix nil target panic by\n[@&#8203;aha-jansen](https://redirect.github.com/aha-jansen)\n([#&#8203;1079](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1079))\n- jsonrpc2: wrap write error in server-closing error by\n[@&#8203;Tethys0](https://redirect.github.com/Tethys0)\n([#&#8203;1186](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1186))\n- internal/jsonrpc2: plumb cancellation cause through request context by\n[@&#8203;aha-jansen](https://redirect.github.com/aha-jansen)\n([#&#8203;1103](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1103))\n- mcp: preserve single-request batch responses by\n[@&#8203;wmh123wmh1](https://redirect.github.com/wmh123wmh1)\n([#&#8203;1214](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1214))\n- mcp: don't mutate caller params on multi-round-trip retries by\n[@&#8203;yhxlele](https://redirect.github.com/yhxlele)\n([#&#8203;1145](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1145))\n- mcp: do not check metatada on notifications by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1215](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1215))\n- fix: only subscribe when server advertises capability by\n[@&#8203;yarolegovich](https://redirect.github.com/yarolegovich)\n([#&#8203;1221](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1221))\n- mcp: tolerate 404 on subscriptions/listen in stateless mode by\n[@&#8203;smlx](https://redirect.github.com/smlx)\n([#&#8203;1193](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1193))\n- mcp: keep request log levels scoped to each request by\n[@&#8203;jstar0](https://redirect.github.com/jstar0)\n([#&#8203;1168](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1168))\n- mcp: add docs for tier 1 assessment by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1195](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1195))\n- docs: make the protocol.md table of contents resolve by\n[@&#8203;tonydzi](https://redirect.github.com/tonydzi)\n([#&#8203;1196](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1196))\n- docs: fix the streamable client snippet to use (\\*Client).Connect by\n[@&#8203;tonydzi](https://redirect.github.com/tonydzi)\n([#&#8203;1142](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1142))\n- docs: quick start `go get` leaves the module unbuildable by\n[@&#8203;tonydzi](https://redirect.github.com/tonydzi)\n([#&#8203;1148](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1148))\n- docs: fix four dead links to the Multi Round-Trip Requests section by\n[@&#8203;tonydzi](https://redirect.github.com/tonydzi)\n([#&#8203;1159](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1159))\n- mcp: fix typo in protocol version comment by\n[@&#8203;latent-9](https://redirect.github.com/latent-9)\n([#&#8203;1156](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1156))\n- mcp: fix ListChanged doc comments on server capabilities by\n[@&#8203;qhzhu](https://redirect.github.com/qhzhu)\n([#&#8203;1219](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1219))\n- mcp: add ServerSession.NotifyElicitationComplete by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1194](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1194))\n- mcp: update conformance tests by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1231](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1231))\n- Disable scheduled nightly runs on forks by\n[@&#8203;IAmSurajBobade](https://redirect.github.com/IAmSurajBobade)\n([#&#8203;1083](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1083))\n- auth: add ScopeFilter hook to AuthorizationCodeHandlerConfig by\n[@&#8203;toabctl](https://redirect.github.com/toabctl)\n([#&#8203;1044](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1044))\n- auth: validate unadvertised RFC 9207 iss instead of rejecting it by\n[@&#8203;asjdf](https://redirect.github.com/asjdf)\n([#&#8203;1187](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1187))\n- mcp: prevent leaks of ServerSession on StatefulServer by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1137](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1137))\n- mcp: avoid Client.Connect leaks by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1158](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1158))\n- mcp: resolve deadlock on serverSession.Close() with\nsubscriptionsListen call by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1166](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1166))\n- mcp: prune completed listen request IDs from the session by\n[@&#8203;latent-9](https://redirect.github.com/latent-9)\n([#&#8203;1190](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1190))\n- mcp: bound streamable Close DELETE so a silent peer cannot hang\nteardown by [@&#8203;LPX-E5BD8](https://redirect.github.com/LPX-E5BD8)\n([#&#8203;1184](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1184))\n- mcp: allow asynchronous cancel notification by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1151](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1151))\n- mcp: fix error propagation to prevent session closing by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n([#&#8203;1118](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1118))\n- refactor: remove legacy MCPGODEBUG compatibility for new protocol\nrelease by\n[@&#8203;guglielmo-san](https://redirect.github.com/guglielmo-san)\n- build(deps): bump the codeql-action group with 3 updates by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1122](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1122))\n- build(deps): bump the codeql-action group with 3 updates by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1216](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1216))\n- build(deps): bump `actions/setup-node` from 6.0.0 to 7.0.0 by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1123](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1123))\n- build(deps): bump `actions/setup-python` from 6.3.0 to 7.0.0 by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1124](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1124))\n- build(deps): bump `actions/setup-go` from 6.5.0 to 7.0.0 by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1125](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1125))\n- build(deps): bump `actions/checkout` from 7.0.0 to 7.0.1 by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1126](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1126))\n- build(deps): bump `golang/govulncheck-action` from 1.0.4 to 1.1.0 by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1218](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1218))\n- build(deps): bump `ossf/scorecard-action` from 2.4.3 to 2.4.4 by\n[@&#8203;dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/dependabot)\n([#&#8203;1217](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1217))\n\n#### New Contributors\n\n- [@&#8203;n0liu](https://redirect.github.com/n0liu) made their first\ncontribution in\n[#&#8203;1120](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1120)\n- [@&#8203;arimu1](https://redirect.github.com/arimu1) made their first\ncontribution in\n[#&#8203;1127](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1127)\n- [@&#8203;tonydzi](https://redirect.github.com/tonydzi) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;1142](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1142)\n- [@&#8203;latent-9](https://redirect.github.com/latent-9) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;1156](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1156)\n- [@&#8203;jstar0](https://redirect.github.com/jstar0) made their first\ncontribution in\n[#&#8203;1168](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1168)\n- [@&#8203;gwyszynski-sa](https://redirect.github.com/gwyszynski-sa)\nmade their first contribution in\n[#&#8203;1163](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1163)\n- [@&#8203;aha-jansen](https://redirect.github.com/aha-jansen) made\ntheir first contribution in\n[#&#8203;1103](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1103)\n- [@&#8203;PratikDhanave](https://redirect.github.com/PratikDhanave)\nmade their first contribution in\n[#&#8203;1132](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1132)\n- [@&#8203;LPX-E5BD8](https://redirect.github.com/LPX-E5BD8) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;1184](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1184)\n- [@&#8203;asjdf](https://redirect.github.com/asjdf) made their first\ncontribution in\n[#&#8203;1187](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1187)\n- [@&#8203;Tethys0](https://redirect.github.com/Tethys0) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;1186](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1186)\n- [@&#8203;wmh123wmh1](https://redirect.github.com/wmh123wmh1) made\ntheir first contribution in\n[#&#8203;1214](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1214)\n- [@&#8203;yhxlele](https://redirect.github.com/yhxlele) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;1145](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1145)\n- [@&#8203;qhzhu](https://redirect.github.com/qhzhu) made their first\ncontribution in\n[#&#8203;1219](https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/pull/1219)\n\n**Full Changelog**:\n<https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/compare/v1.7.0...v1.8.0-pre.1>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>urfave/cli (github.com/urfave/cli/v3)</summary>\n\n###\n[`v3.13.0`](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/releases/tag/v3.13.0)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/compare/v3.12.0...v3.13.0)\n\n#### What's Changed\n\n- Trim the key of a map flag when TrimSpace is set by\n[@&#8203;youdie006](https://redirect.github.com/youdie006) in\n[#&#8203;2431](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2431)\n- Fix inverse bool flag counting with an external counter by\n[@&#8203;jakezwang](https://redirect.github.com/jakezwang) in\n[#&#8203;2432](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2432)\n- feat: add Deprecated field to flags and commands by\n[@&#8203;anandghegde](https://redirect.github.com/anandghegde) in\n[#&#8203;2429](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2429)\n- fix: parse single-rune Unicode flags by\n[@&#8203;znnnnnnn-wil](https://redirect.github.com/znnnnnnn-wil) in\n[#&#8203;2434](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2434)\n\n#### New Contributors\n\n- [@&#8203;jakezwang](https://redirect.github.com/jakezwang) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;2432](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2432)\n- [@&#8203;anandghegde](https://redirect.github.com/anandghegde) made\ntheir first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2429](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2429)\n- [@&#8203;znnnnnnn-wil](https://redirect.github.com/znnnnnnn-wil) made\ntheir first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2434](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2434)\n\n**Full Changelog**:\n<https://github.com/urfave/cli/compare/v3.12.0...v3.13.0>\n\n###\n[`v3.12.0`](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/releases/tag/v3.12.0)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/compare/v3.11.0...v3.12.0)\n\n#### What's Changed\n\n- feat: add Command.ArgValidator for tree-wide argument validation by\n[@&#8203;dearchap](https://redirect.github.com/dearchap) in\n[#&#8203;2377](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2377)\n- Single-value arguments can be marked as required by\n[@&#8203;idelchi](https://redirect.github.com/idelchi) in\n[#&#8203;2393](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2393)\n- docs: clarify that named Arguments are excluded from cmd.Args() by\n[@&#8203;dearchap](https://redirect.github.com/dearchap) in\n[#&#8203;2411](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2411)\n- fix: never run command action on shell completion past a double dash\nby [@&#8203;dearchap](https://redirect.github.com/dearchap) in\n[#&#8203;2412](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2412)\n- chore(deps): bump github.com/stretchr/testify from 1.11.1 to 1.12.0 by\n[@&#8203;app/dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/app/dependabot) in\n[#&#8203;2413](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2413)\n- Support custom FlagStringer for MutuallyExclusiveFlags by\n[@&#8203;SHIVANSHGARG07](https://redirect.github.com/SHIVANSHGARG07) in\n[#&#8203;2414](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2414)\n- Add TextFlag for encoding.TextMarshaler/TextUnmarshaler values by\n[@&#8203;ChrisJr404](https://redirect.github.com/ChrisJr404) in\n[#&#8203;2415](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2415)\n- chore(deps): bump github.com/stretchr/testify from 1.12.0 to 1.12.1 by\n[@&#8203;app/dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/app/dependabot) in\n[#&#8203;2416](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2416)\n- chore(deps): bump the python-packages group with 2 updates by\n[@&#8203;app/dependabot](https://redirect.github.com/app/dependabot) in\n[#&#8203;2417](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2417)\n- Show inherited persistent flags in child help by\n[@&#8203;justadityaraj](https://redirect.github.com/justadityaraj) in\n[#&#8203;2421](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2421)\n- fix: preserve whitespace in positional arguments by\n[@&#8203;lenamonj](https://redirect.github.com/lenamonj) in\n[#&#8203;2423](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2423)\n- fix: preserve whitespace in equals-form flag values by\n[@&#8203;BenYang12](https://redirect.github.com/BenYang12) in\n[#&#8203;2425](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2425)\n- fix: complete subcommand flags after positional arguments by\n[@&#8203;fzlzjerry](https://redirect.github.com/fzlzjerry) in\n[#&#8203;2426](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2426)\n- Fix a year-less timestamp layout losing January 1 by\n[@&#8203;youdie006](https://redirect.github.com/youdie006) in\n[#&#8203;2427](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2427)\n- docs: add go-size-analyzer, module version, and reflection by\n[@&#8203;imsumedhaa](https://redirect.github.com/imsumedhaa) in\n[#&#8203;2428](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2428)\n\n#### New Contributors\n\n- [@&#8203;idelchi](https://redirect.github.com/idelchi) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;2393](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2393)\n- [@&#8203;SHIVANSHGARG07](https://redirect.github.com/SHIVANSHGARG07)\nmade their first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2414](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2414)\n- [@&#8203;ChrisJr404](https://redirect.github.com/ChrisJr404) made\ntheir first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2415](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2415)\n- [@&#8203;justadityaraj](https://redirect.github.com/justadityaraj)\nmade their first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2421](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2421)\n- [@&#8203;lenamonj](https://redirect.github.com/lenamonj) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;2423](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2423)\n- [@&#8203;BenYang12](https://redirect.github.com/BenYang12) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;2425](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2425)\n- [@&#8203;youdie006](https://redirect.github.com/youdie006) made their\nfirst contribution in\n[#&#8203;2427](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2427)\n- [@&#8203;imsumedhaa](https://redirect.github.com/imsumedhaa) made\ntheir first contribution in\n[#&#8203;2428](https://redirect.github.com/urfave/cli/pull/2428)\n\n**Full Changelog**:\n<https://github.com/urfave/cli/compare/v3.11.0...v3.12.0>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>grpc/grpc-go (google.golang.org/grpc)</summary>\n\n###\n[`v1.84.0`](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/releases/tag/v1.84.0):\nRelease 1.84.0\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/compare/v1.83.2...v1.84.0)\n\n### Behavior Changes\n\n- stats/otel: The `grpc.lb.pick_first.*` metrics have been removed and\nreplaced with `grpc.subchannel.*` metrics. See [gRFC\nA94](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/proposal/blob/master/A94-subchannel-otel-metrics.md)\nfor more details.\n([#&#8203;9215](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9215))\n\n### New Features\n\n- xds: Add support for `contains_match` in route header matchers.\n([#&#8203;9223](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9223))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- client: Fix a bug where a `ClientConn` could get permanently stuck in\nIDLE when an RPC was canceled during stream creation. Previously, such\ncancellations triggered stream cleanup twice, corrupting the channel's\nidleness state and causing subsequent RPCs to fail with deadline\nexceeded errors.\n([#&#8203;9191](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9191))\n- Special Thanks:\n[@&#8203;utkuozdemir](https://redirect.github.com/utkuozdemir)\n- client: Fix a bug where non-gRPC HTTP responses ending with an empty\nDATA frame failed the RPC with status code `Internal` instead of\npreserving the HTTP-mapped status code and response body.\n([#&#8203;9217](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9217))\n- Special Thanks:\n[@&#8203;chengxilo](https://redirect.github.com/chengxilo)\n- credentials: Validate metadata returned by per-RPC credentials,\nfailing the RPC with status code `Internal` if invalid keys or values\nare found. Previously, invalid metadata from credentials was sent to the\nserver in outgoing HTTP/2 requests.\n([#&#8203;9202](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9202))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;buger](https://redirect.github.com/buger)\n- credentials/sts: Prevent potential token leakage by disallowing HTTP\nredirects during STS token exchange. Previously, 3xx redirects were\nfollowed automatically, replaying the request body containing\nauthentication tokens to the redirect destination.\n([#&#8203;9299](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9299))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n- randomsubsetting: Ignore endpoints that contain no addresses.\nPreviously, this could cause the policy to panic while computing hashes.\n([#&#8203;9259](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9259))\n- Special Thanks:\n[@&#8203;fallintoplace](https://redirect.github.com/fallintoplace)\n- stats/otel: Ensure method names are populated in trace spans when\nmetrics are disabled. Previously, running with tracing enabled and\nmetrics disabled resulted in server trace spans lacking the RPC method\nname (recording only \"Recv.\").\n([#&#8203;9262](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9262))\n- transport: Return `io.ErrUnexpectedEOF` when EOF is encountered after\npartial header or message body reads. Previously, partial reads could\nreturn a plain `io.EOF`, failing to distinguish truncated data from a\nclean end of stream.\n([#&#8203;9204](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9204))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;buger](https://redirect.github.com/buger)\n- transport: Validate metadata supplied by balancers (in\n`PickResult.Metadata`) and resolver addresses, failing the RPC with\nstatus code `Internal` if invalid keys or values are found. Previously,\ninvalid metadata from these sources was sent to the server in outgoing\nHTTP/2 requests.\n([#&#8203;9203](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9203))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;buger](https://redirect.github.com/buger)\n- xds: Fix a rare corner case that could prevent a cluster from being\nremoved when it is no longer in use.\n([#&#8203;9140](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9140))\n- xds: Fix panic during route matching for routes containing header\nmatchers with empty `exact_match` strings.\n([#&#8203;9223](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9223))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n- xds: Reject routes containing header matchers with empty\n`prefix_match` or `suffix_match` strings. Previously, this caused a\npanic during route matching.\n([#&#8203;9223](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9223))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n- xds: Fix EDS drop policies being applied at a much lower rate than\nconfigured due to an integer overflow.\n([#&#8203;9257](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9257))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n- xds: Reject EDS resources containing drop policies with unsupported\ndenominators. Previously, such resources caused the client to panic when\ncalculating drop rates.\n([#&#8203;9218](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9218))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n- xds/rbac: Reject RBAC configurations containing nested `Principal` or\n`Permission` rules with `:scheme` or `grpc-` prefixed header matchers.\nPreviously, such configurations could cause DENY policies to fail open.\n([#&#8203;9258](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9258))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n- xds/rbac: Rewrite `host` header matchers to `:authority` in nested\n`Principal` and `Permission` rules. Previously, this rewrite only\napplied to top-level rules, causing nested `host` matchers to never\nmatch incoming requests and DENY policies to fail open.\n([#&#8203;9258](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9258))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n- xds/rbac: Reject `CidrRanges` with an unset prefix length. Previously,\nan omitted `prefix_len` field caused a panic during RBAC configuration\nparsing.\n([#&#8203;9250](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9250))\n  - Special Thanks: [@&#8203;nvxbug](https://redirect.github.com/nvxbug)\n\n### Performance Improvements\n\n- transport: Avoid a heap allocation when flushing shared write buffers.\n([#&#8203;9233](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9233))\n- Special Thanks:\n[@&#8203;zaidoon1](https://redirect.github.com/zaidoon1)\n- credentials/alts: Support dynamic frame size negotiation and add the\n`GRPC_GO_EXPERIMENTAL_ALTS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE` environment variable (default\n4KiB, max 512KiB) to configure the maximum ALTS record frame size.\n([#&#8203;9268](https://redirect.github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/9268))\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Configuration\n\n📅 **Schedule**: (in timezone Australia/Sydney)\n\n- Branch creation\n  - \"before 6am on monday\"\n- Automerge\n  - At any time (no schedule defined)\n\n🚦 **Automerge**: Disabled by config. Please merge this manually once you\nare satisfied.\n\n♻ **Rebasing**: Whenever PR becomes conflicted, or you tick the\nrebase/retry checkbox.\n\n👻 **Immortal**: This PR will be recreated if closed unmerged. Get\n[config\nhelp](https://redirect.github.com/renovatebot/renovate/discussions) if\nthat's undesired.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] <!-- rebase-check -->If you want to rebase/retry this PR, check\nthis box\n\n---\n\nThis PR was generated by [Mend Renovate](https://mend.io/renovate/).\nView the [repository job\nlog](https://developer.mend.io/github/google/osv-scanner).\n\n<!--renovate-debug:eyJjcmVhdGVkSW5WZXIiOiI0NC43MS4wIiwidXBkYXRlZEluVmVyIjoiNDQuMTEyLjAiLCJ0YXJnZXRCcmFuY2giOiJtYWluIiwibGFiZWxzIjpbImRlcGVuZGVuY2llcyJdfQ==-->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Rex P <rexpan@google.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-02T05:16:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/osv-scanner/commits/1b86129be1f0285c403616cb362ac188de676c6e","html_url":"https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/commit/1b86129be1f0285c403616cb362ac188de676c6e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/osv-scanner/commits/1b86129be1f0285c403616cb362ac188de676c6e/comments","author":{"login":"renovate-bot","id":25180681,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MTgwNjgx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25180681?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/renovate-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"eb6f0e10e76b9fac503af73556cba2528773062d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/osv-scanner/commits/eb6f0e10e76b9fac503af73556cba2528773062d","html_url":"https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/commit/eb6f0e10e76b9fac503af73556cba2528773062d"}],"stats":{"total":27,"additions":10,"deletions":17},"files":[{"sha":"88a48ec70c1edba45bc28cf99c9cbd2f12086fee","filename":"cmd/osv-scanner/mcp/__snapshots__/integration_test.snap","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":8,"changes":9,"blob_url":"https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/blob/1b86129be1f0285c403616cb362ac188de676c6e/cmd%2Fosv-scanner%2Fmcp%2F__snapshots__%2Fintegration_test.snap","raw_url":"https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/raw/1b86129be1f0285c403616cb362ac188de676c6e/cmd%2Fosv-scanner%2Fmcp%2F__snapshots__%2Fintegration_test.snap","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/osv-scanner/contents/cmd%2Fosv-scanner%2Fmcp%2F__snapshots__%2Fintegration_test.snap?ref=1b86129be1f0285c403616cb362ac188de676c6e","patch":"@@ -1,19 +1,12 @@\n \n [TestIntegration_MCP_SSE_Subprocess/GetVulnerabilityDetails - 1]\n {\n-  \"_meta\": {\n-    \"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo\": {\n-      \"name\": \"OSV-Scanner\",\n-      \"version\": \"2.6.0\"\n-    }\n-  },\n   \"content\": [\n     {\n       \"type\": \"text\",\n       \"text\": \"{\\n  \\\"schema_version\\\": \\\"1.7.3\\\",\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"GO-2023-1558\\\",\\n  \\\"published\\\": \\\"2023-02-14T19:41:21Z\\\",\\n  \\\"modified\\\": \\\"2024-05-20T16:03:47Z\\\",\\n  \\\"aliases\\\": [\\\"CVE-2023-23626\\\", \\\"GHSA-2h6c-j3gf-xp9r\\\"],\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Denial of service via malformed size parameters in github.com/ipfs/go-bitfield\\\",\\n  \\\"details\\\": \\\"When feeding untrusted user input into the size parameter of NewBitfield and FromBytes functions, an attacker can trigger panics.\\\\n\\\\nThis happens when the size is a not a multiple of 8 or is negative.\\\\n\\\\nA workaround is to ensure size%8 == 0 \\u0026\\u0026 size \\u003e= 0 yourself before calling NewBitfield or FromBytes.\\\",\\n  \\\"affected\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"package\\\": {\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"github.com/ipfs/go-bitfield\\\",\\n        \\\"ecosystem\\\": \\\"Go\\\",\\n        \\\"purl\\\": \\\"pkg:golang/github.com/ipfs/go-bitfield\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"ranges\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"SEMVER\\\",\\n          \\\"events\\\": [\\n            {\\n              \\\"introduced\\\": \\\"0\\\"\\n            },\\n            {\\n              \\\"fixed\\\": \\\"1.1.0\\\"\\n            }\\n          ]\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"ecosystem_specific\\\": {\\n        \\\"imports\\\": [\\n          {\\n            \\\"path\\\": \\\"github.com/ipfs/go-bitfield\\\",\\n            \\\"symbols\\\": [\\\"FromBytes\\\", \\\"NewBitfield\\\"]\\n          }\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \\\"database_specific\\\": {\\n        \\\"source\\\": \\\"https://vuln.go.dev/ID/GO-2023-1558.json\\\"\\n      }\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"references\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"ADVISORY\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/ipfs/go-bitfield/security/advisories/GHSA-2h6c-j3gf-xp9r\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"FIX\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://github.com/ipfs/go-bitfield/commit/5e1d256fe043fc4163343ccca83862c69c52e579\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"database_specific\\\": {\\n    \\\"review_status\\\": \\\"REVIEWED\\\",\\n    \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2023-1558\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"credits\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Jorropo\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\"\n     }\n-  ],\n-  \"resultType\": \"complete\"\n+  ]\n }\n ---\n "},{"sha":"ef98e3df8379d17778114be9579634635ef48b92","filename":"go.mod","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":3,"changes":6,"blob_url":"https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/blob/1b86129be1f0285c403616cb362ac188de676c6e/go.mod","raw_url":"https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/raw/1b86129be1f0285c403616cb362ac188de676c6e/go.mod","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/osv-scanner/contents/go.mod?ref=1b86129be1f0285c403616cb362ac188de676c6e","patch":"@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ require (\n \tgithub.com/google/osv-scalibr v0.5.4-0.20261001171654-3690fe35c1fe\n \tgithub.com/ianlancetaylor/demangle v0.0.0-20260724033716-83e58baca724\n \tgithub.com/jedib0t/go-pretty/v6 v6.8.3\n-\tgithub.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk v1.7.0\n+\tgithub.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk v1.8.0\n \tgithub.com/opencontainers/go-digest v1.0.0\n \tgithub.com/ossf/osv-schema/bindings/go v0.0.0-20260902031056-b388a18021a3\n \tgithub.com/owenrumney/go-sarif/v3 v3.3.1\n@@ -23,11 +23,11 @@ require (\n \tgithub.com/tidwall/gjson v1.19.0\n \tgithub.com/tidwall/pretty v1.2.1\n \tgithub.com/tidwall/sjson v1.2.5\n-\tgithub.com/urfave/cli/v3 v3.11.0\n+\tgithub.com/urfave/cli/v3 v3.13.0\n \tgo.yaml.in/yaml/v4 v4.0.0-rc.6\n \tgolang.org/x/term v0.46.0\n \tgolang.org/x/vuln v1.6.0\n-\tgoogle.golang.org/grpc v1.83.2\n+\tgoogle.golang.org/grpc v1.84.0\n \tgoogle.golang.org/protobuf v1.36.12\n \tgopkg.in/dnaeon/go-vcr.v4 v4.0.7\n \tosv.dev/bindings/go v0.0.0-20260805021707-3a57b89df3b6"},{"sha":"16218b05d9de41bf372c9daaba35cc2e99d3931f","filename"